Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Warn when VSync is enabled without overriding the user's preference.
Dependencies: 44_AUDIO_PACED_DEFAULT.todo.

Purpose:
Explain the known audio risk at the moment someone enables native VSync.
Keep the existing VSync-off default, saved choices and fast-forward behavior.

Tasks:
- [x] Add an immediate warning to the existing native-panel notification host.
- [x] Explain crackling, stutter/dropouts and how to restore audio-paced playback.
- [x] Re-warn when opening settings with an explicitly saved enabled preference.
- [x] Keep native method behavior, choice and preference persistence intact.
- [x] Complete focused browser qualification and inspect the actual warning.
- [ ] Publish through the normal hosted gate and independently verify delivery.
- [ ] Update affected documentation, final evidence and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
- The actual native VSync menu shows the warning immediately upon enabling.
- Warning severity and text are visible inside the open settings dialog.
- Explicit enabled choices remain enabled and remembered; no forced reset.
- Disabling/default-off does not create an enabled warning.
- Dismissal is respected until a new enable or enabled-panel opening.
- Existing native settings and speed/VSync coordination remain functional.
- Risk is described as possible audio starvation, not universal guaranteed failure.

Completion evidence:
- Actual new native-menu regression fails old implementation: notice stays hidden.
- Initial hook at EJS_ready fails because changeSettingOption is not installed yet.
  Move the hook to EJS_onGameStart, alongside existing runtime adapter setup.
- Native settings/lifecycle regression passes after that correction.
- New persistence assertion initially reads before async settings close completes;
  wait for the actual persisted VSync value rather than changing product behavior.
- Focused speed sample once reads 3.84x at selected 2x; preserve the clock bounds
  and record subsequent qualification separately. No production timing changes.
- The new test initially tries dismissing a notification that is correctly hidden
  after reload. Assert that hidden state before opening the enabled panel instead.
- Final three focused browser cases pass in 59.1 seconds: actual enable warning,
  persistence/reopening/disable/re-enable, existing native lifecycle/settings,
  and fast-forward/native VSync cartridge-clock coordination.
- Syntax/build and all 11 unit cases pass; actual warning crop visually inspected.
- Remaining browser, publication and human acceptance are not implied.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-05: User requests a notification explaining what enabling VSync risks.
